From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 21:45:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: compare intf_type against INTF_DSI, not the DRM
 encoder type

The cmd-mode DCS/frame interlock added in "drm/msm/dsi: serialize cmd-mode
DCS transfers against frame kickoff" hooks dpu_encoder_kickoff() behind

	if (dpu_enc->disp_info.intf_type == DRM_MODE_ENCODER_DSI)

but disp_info.intf_type is an enum dpu_intf_type, where INTF_DSI is 0x1.
DRM_MODE_ENCODER_DSI is 6, from a completely unrelated uapi enum.  The
condition is therefore never true, msm_dsi_cmd_kickoff_begin() has never once
been called, frame_pending was never set, and the entire interlock -- plus the
dsi-collide detector that reads the same state -- has been dead code since it
was written.  Everything around it already uses the right enum
(dpu_encoder.c:287, :649).

Measured with kprobes on a Pixel 2 XL during a backlight sweep, 6 s:

	dpu_encoder_kickoff                 = 69
	dpu_encoder_trigger_kickoff_pending = 69
	msm_dsi_cmd_kickoff_begin           =  0
	frames (vsync delta)                = 94

and over 448 DCS transfers in a separate run the interlock blocked exactly
zero times, while the panel corrupted into full-screen noise banded at DSC
slice boundaries -- the signature panel-lg-sw43402.c predicts for a DCS write
landing inside a frame.

Also require is_cmd_mode.  In video mode the DPU streams continuously, there
is no CMD_MDP_DONE to retire a frame, and arming the interlock there would
make every DCS write wait out its 100 ms timeout.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
index 2f81b63f77ff..55623dbed849 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
@@ -2164,7 +2164,8 @@ void dpu_encoder_kickoff(struct drm_encoder *drm_enc)
 	 * which triggers CTL_START under enc_spinlock (atomic). No-op unless
 	 * the dsi host has cmd_frame_serialize set.
 	 */
-	if (dpu_enc->disp_info.intf_type == DRM_MODE_ENCODER_DSI)
+	if (dpu_enc->disp_info.is_cmd_mode &&
+	    dpu_enc->disp_info.intf_type == INTF_DSI)
 		msm_dsi_cmd_kickoff_begin();
 
 	/* All phys encs are ready to go, trigger the kickoff */
